\f3\fs28 \cf6 \cb7 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
I\'92d split the five as three aggregation-focused and two cellular-phenotype-focused. Aggregation is the more direct SOD1 readout; cellular toxicity is downstream and easier to confound with expression, folding, or metal-handling defects.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb7 By cellular toxicity, I mean a reproducible loss of motor-neuron health\'97reduced viability, neurite degeneration, or impaired stress tolerance\'97at comparable SOD1 expression, with normal catalytic activity and no evidence that the mutation merely causes gross misfolding. I\'92d test aggregation and toxicity for all five, but use that 3:2 split for the experimental emphasis. Do you have a motor-neuron viability/neurite assay, or only a general cell line?\
\
3. You\'92re right\'97we had not set a threshold. By \'93preserve function,\'94 I meant that the mutant should retain near-wild-type catalytic activity and metal handling, rather than merely looking folded in the model.\cf6 \cb1 \
\cf6 \cb7 For a defensible rule, I\'92d predefine something like at least 80% of wild-type dismutase activity, with comparable expression and solubility; anything below that becomes a functional-loss mutant, not an aggregation/toxicity-specific probe. \
\
4. And 5. We are making our own structure, correct?\
\
6. Chose A4V.\
\
7. No, that we need to determine.\
\
8. Yes it\'92s not and we need to double check how much it is both in the owners and our created newly folded protein.\
\
9. I guess we will get some more info when we fold the protein ourselves?\
 10. \'92d test them in stages, against wild-type SOD1, the empty-vector control, and A4V as the disruptive reference:\cf6 \cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa47\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf6 \cb7 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Expression and stability: verify comparable protein production, solubility, and intact size by immunoblotting and soluble/insoluble fractionation. A toxic result is uninterpretable if the mutant is simply absent or grossly unstable.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb7 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Catalytic function: measure superoxide-dismutase activity and, where possible, metal loading. I\'92d classify a candidate as function-preserving only if it retains at least 80% of wild-type activity.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb7 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Aggregation: quantify insoluble or high-molecular-weight SOD1 by sedimentation or size-based analysis, then confirm selected results by microscopy or a second orthogonal assay.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb7 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Cellular effects: express matched amounts in motor-neuron-like cells and measure viability, neurite length/branching, and stress sensitivity. I\'92d call toxicity real only if it is reproducible, dose-related, and not explained by poor expression or loss of catalytic activity.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0\cb7 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Interpretation: a useful exploratory mutant retains \uc0\u8805 80% activity and comparable expression, yet changes aggregation or cellular health relative to wild type. A4V should show that the assay can detect destabilization, not serve as a clean mechanistic probe.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \cb7 I\'92d run the activity and expression checks before spending effort on the cell assay. \
\
