 \cf5 - \cf4 Its chemistry plausibly affects abnormal protein\'96protein, membrane, mitochondrial, or   \
   stress-related interactions.                                                            \
 \cf5 - \cf4 The protein\'92s functional context supports that type of interaction.                     \
                                                                                           \
 But structure alone cannot establish that the mutation causes cellular toxicity. The      \
 appropriate distinction is:                                                               \
                                                                                           \
 \cf5 - 
\f2\b \cf4 Structural evidence:
\f1\b0  \'93This residue is a plausible candidate for testing effects on      \
   abnormal cellular interactions.\'94                                                        \
 \cf5 - 
\f2\b \cf4 Functional hypothesis:
\f1\b0  \'93Changing this exposed surface chemistry may alter interactions  \
   associated with cellular stress.\'94                                                       \
 \cf5 - 
\f2\b \cf4 Experimental conclusion:
\f1\b0  \'93The mutation caused cellular toxicity,\'94 only after matched    \
   expression, stability/solubility, catalytic activity, and a suitable cellular assay     \
   show a reproducible effect.                                                             \
